s":53},"checked locking. The canonical singleton pattern.\n",[43,1391,1392,1394,1396,1398,1400,1403,1406,1409,1412,1415,1417,1419,1422,1424,1427,1429,1432,1434,1437,1439,1442,1444,1447,1450,1453,1456,1459,1462,1464,1466,1468,1471,1474,1476,1479,1481],{"class":45,"line":262},[43,1393,242],{"class":49},[43,1395,1357],{"class":49},[43,1397,1360],{"class":53},[43,1399,174],{"class":49},[43,1401,1402],{"class":53},": prefer a ",[43,1404,1405],{"class":150},"`map`",[43,1407,1408],{"class":49}," +",[43,1410,1411],{"class":150}," `RWMutex`",[43,1413,1414],{"class":53}," over ",[43,1416,1277],{"class":150},[43,1418,1370],{"class":49},[43,1420,1421],{"class":53}," general concurrent maps — ",[43,1423,1277],{"class":150},[43,1425,1426],{"class":53}," is optimized ",[43,1428,401],{"class":49},[43,1430,1431],{"class":53}," write",[43,1433,242],{"class":49},[43,1435,1436],{"class":53},"rarely",[43,1438,225],{"class":49},[43,1440,1441],{"class":53},"read",[43,1443,242],{"class":49},[43,1445,1446],{"class":53},"many (caches) and uses ",[43,1448,1449],{"class":150},"`any`",[43,1451,1452],{"class":53}," (no ",[43,1454,1455],{"class":49},"type",[43,1457,1458],{"class":53}," safety). A generic ",[43,1460,1461],{"class":49},"map",[43,1463,1408],{"class":49},[43,1465,1411],{"class":150},[43,1467,957],{"class":53},[43,1469,1470],{"class":49},"type-",[43,1472,1473],{"class":53},"safe and often faster ",[43,1475,401],{"class":49},[43,1477,1478],{"class":53}," balanced read",[43,1480,225],{"class":49},[43,1482,1483],{"class":53},"write workloads.\n",[43,1485,1486],{"class":45,"line":268},[43,1487,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1489,1490,1493,1495],{"class":45,"line":274},[43,1491,1492],{"class":53},"## ⚠️ Edge Cases ",[43,1494,754],{"class":49},[43,1496,1497],{"class":53}," Gotchas\n",[43,1499,1500],{"class":45,"line":280},[43,1501,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1503,1504,1506,1508,1511,1513,1515,1518,1520,1523,1526,1528,1531,1533],{"class":45,"line":285},[43,1505,242],{"class":49},[43,1507,1357],{"class":49},[43,1509,1510],{"class":53},"Copying a ",[43,1512,168],{"class":150},[43,1514,225],{"class":49},[43,1516,1517],{"class":150},"`WaitGroup`",[43,1519,225],{"class":49},[43,1521,1522],{"class":150},"`Once`",[43,1524,1525],{"class":53}," is a bug",[43,1527,174],{"class":49},[43,1529,1530],{"class":53},": these have internal state that mustn",[43,1532,1288],{"class":150},[43,1534,1535],{"class":1291},"t be copied. `go vet` catches this (\"assignment copies lock value\"). Pass them by pointer.\n",[43,1537,1538],{"class":45,"line":290},[43,1539,1540],{"class":1291},"- **Forgetting `Unlock`**: a `Lock` without `Unlock` (e.g., an early return) deadlocks. Use `defer`.\n",[43,1542,1543,1546,1548,1551,1553,1556,1558],{"class":45,"line":296},[43,1544,1545],{"class":1291},"- **`RWMutex` can starve writers**: if readers continuously hold `RLock`, a writer may wait indefinitely (Go",[43,1547,1288],{"class":150},[43,1549,1550],{"class":53},"s RWMutex has anti",[43,1552,242],{"class":49},[43,1554,1555],{"class":53},"starvation, but be aware). For write",[43,1557,242],{"class":49},[43,1559,1560],{"class":53},"heavy work, use a plain Mutex.\n",[43,1562,1563,1565,1567,1570,1573,1575,1578,1581,1584,1586,1589,1591,1594,1596,1598,1600,1602,1605],{"class":45,"line":302},[43,1564,242],{"class":49},[43,1566,1357],{"class":49},[43,1568,1569],{"class":150},"`WaitGroup.Add`",[43,1571,1572],{"class":53}," inside the goroutine is a race",[43,1574,174],{"class":49},[43,1576,1577],{"class":53},": ",[43,1579,1580],{"class":150},"`go func() { wg.Add(1); ... }()`",[43,1582,1583],{"class":53}," — ",[43,1585,585],{"class":150},[43,1587,1588],{"class":53}," may see counter ",[43,1590,837],{"class":410},[43,1592,1593],{"class":53}," before ",[43,1595,574],{"class":150},[43,1597,1340],{"class":53},[43,1599,574],{"class":150},[43,1601,1593],{"class":53},[43,1603,1604],{"class":150},"`go`",[43,1606,1607],{"class":53},".\n",[43,1609,1610,1612,1614,1617,1620,1622,1625,1627,1630,1632,1635,1638],{"class":45,"line":308},[43,1611,242],{"class":49},[43,1613,1357],{"class":49},[43,1615,1616],{"class":150},"`Once.Do`",[43,1618,1619],{"class":53}," blocks concurrent callers",[43,1621,174],{"class":49},[43,1623,1624],{"class":53},": the first call runs ",[43,1626,1348],{"class":150},[43,1628,1629],{"class":53},"; other callers block until it completes. If ",[43,1631,1348],{"class":150},[43,1633,1634],{"class":53}," is slow, all concurrent ",[43,1636,1637],{"class":150},"`Do`",[43,1639,1640],{"class":53}," calls wait.\n",[43,1642,1643,1645,1647,1649,1652,1654,1657,1659],{"class":45,"line":314},[43,1644,242],{"class":49},[43,1646,1357],{"class":49},[43,1648,996],{"class":150},[43,1650,1651],{"class":53}," objects can be reclaimed",[43,1653,174],{"class":49},[43,1655,1656],{"class":53},": between GC cycles, pooled objects may be freed. Don",[43,1658,1288],{"class":150},[43,1660,1661],{"class":1291},"t store state you need to persist. Reset objects before `Put` (so the next `Get` gets a clean state).\n",[43,1663,1664],{"class":45,"line":319},[43,1665,1666],{"class":1291},"- **`sync.Map` is not generic**: it uses `any` — you lose type safety (type-assert on `Load`). For type safety, use a `map` + `RWMutex`.\n",[43,1668,1669],{"class":45,"line":324},[43,1670,1671],{"class":1291},"- **`Cond.Wait` must be called with the mutex locked**: `Wait` unlocks, waits, re-locks. Calling it without holding the lock is a runtime error (or undefined behavior).\n",[43,1673,1674],{"class":45,"line":330},[43,1675,1676],{"class":1291},"- **`Cond` spurious wakeups**: `Wait` can wake without `Signal`\u002F`Broadcast`. Always check the condition in a loop: `for !condition { cond.Wait() }`.\n",[43,1678,1679,1682,1684,1687,1689],{"class":45,"line":336},[43,1680,1681],{"class":1291},"- **`Pool.New` is called on `Get` from an empty pool**: each `Get` from an empty pool calls `New` (not reused). If `New` is expensive, the pool isn",[43,1683,1288],{"class":150},[43,1685,1686],{"class":53},"t helping ",[43,1688,401],{"class":49},[43,1690,1691],{"class":53}," the first calls.\n",[43,1693,1694],{"class":45,"line":342},[43,1695,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1697,1698],{"class":45,"line":348},[43,1699,1700],{"class":53},"## 🧠 Spot the Bug\n",[43,1702,1703],{"class":45,"line":353},[43,1704,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1706,1707,1710,1713],{"class":45,"line":1044},[43,1708,1709],{"class":53},"A developer protects a counter with a mutex, but ",[43,1711,1712],{"class":150},"`go vet`",[43,1714,1715],{"class":53}," complains:\n",[43,1717,1718],{"class":45,"line":1049},[43,1719,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1721,1722,1724,1726,1728,1730,1732],{"class":45,"line":1054},[43,1723,239],{"class":53},[43,1725,242],{"class":49},[43,1727,245],{"class":53},[43,1729,248],{"class":49},[43,1731,251],{"class":150},[43,1733,144],{"class":53},[43,1735,1736],{"class":45,"line":1060},[43,1737,259],{"class":150},[43,1739,1740],{"class":45,"line":1066},[43,1741,1742],{"class":150},"type Counter struct {\n",[43,1744,1745],{"class":45,"line":1072},[43,1746,1747],{"class":150},"    mu    sync.Mutex\n",[43,1749,1750],{"class":45,"line":1078},[43,1751,1752],{"class":150},"    count int\n",[43,1754,1755],{"class":45,"line":1084},[43,1756,144],{"class":150},[43,1758,1759],{"class":45,"line":1090},[43,1760,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1762,1763],{"class":45,"line":1095},[43,1764,1765],{"class":150},"func increment(c Counter) {   \u002F\u002F ❌ Counter is copied (mu is copied)\n",[43,1767,1769],{"class":45,"line":1768},47,[43,1770,1771],{"class":150},"    c.mu.Lock()\n",[43,1773,1775],{"class":45,"line":1774},48,[43,1776,1777],{"class":150},"    c.count++\n",[43,1779,1781],{"class":45,"line":1780},49,[43,1782,1783],{"class":150},"    c.mu.Unlock()\n",[43,1785,1787],{"class":45,"line":1786},50,[43,1788,144],{"class":150},[43,1790,1792],{"class":45,"line":1791},51,[43,1793,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1795,1797],{"class":45,"line":1796},52,[43,1798,1799],{"class":150},"func main() {\n",[43,1801,1803],{"class":45,"line":1802},53,[43,1804,1805],{"class":150},"    c := Counter{}\n",[43,1807,1809],{"class":45,"line":1808},54,[43,1810,1811],{"class":150},"    go increment(c)\n",[43,1813,1815],{"class":45,"line":1814},55,[43,1816,1811],{"class":150},[43,1818,1820],{"class":45,"line":1819},56,[43,1821,144],{"class":150},[14,1823,1824],{},"::",[14,1826,1827],{},"What's wrong?",[1829,1830,1831,1835,1852,1874,1880,1982,1988],"details",{},[1832,1833,1834],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1836,1837,1840,1841,1844,1845,1848,1849,1851],{},[18,1838,1839],{},"increment(c Counter)"," receives ",[18,1842,1843],{},"Counter"," ",[1117,1846,1847],{},"by value"," — it copies the struct, including the ",[18,1850,28],{},". Each goroutine gets its own copy of the mutex (and the counter), so:",[1853,1854,1855,1868],"ol",{},[1856,1857,1858,1859,1863,1864,1867],"li",{},"The two goroutines lock ",[1860,1861,1862],"em",{},"different"," mutexes — no mutual exclusion (race condition on the original ",[18,1865,1866],{},"c"," if they could reach it, but they're modifying copies anyway).",[1856,1869,1870,1873],{},[18,1871,1872],{},"go vet"," flags \"increment passes lock by value: Counter contains sync.Mutex\" — copying a mutex is a bug.",[14,1875,1876,1877,1879],{},"The fix — pass ",[18,1878,1843],{}," by pointer, and make the method take a pointer receiver:",[35,1881,1883],{"className":37,"code":1882,"language":33,"meta":39,"style":39},"func increment(c *Counter) {\n    c.mu.Lock()\n    defer c.mu.Unlock()\n    c.count++\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n    c := &Counter{}\n    go increment(c)\n    go increment(c)\n}\n",[18,1884,1885,1902,1911,1922,1929,1933,1937,1946,1961,1970,1978],{"__ignoreMap":39},[43,1886,1887,1889,1891,1893,1895,1898,1900],{"class":45,"line":46},[43,1888,97],{"class":49},[43,1890,100],{"class":63},[43,1892,440],{"class":53},[43,1894,1866],{"class":458},[43,1896,1897],{"class":49}," *",[43,1899,1843],{"class":63},[43,1901,465],{"class":53},[43,1903,1904,1907,1909],{"class":45,"line":57},[43,1905,1906],{"class":53},"    c.mu.",[43,1908,112],{"class":63},[43,1910,115],{"class":53},[43,1912,1913,1915,1918,1920],{"class":45,"line":72},[43,1914,121],{"class":49},[43,1916,1917],{"class":53}," c.mu.",[43,1919,127],{"class":63},[43,1921,115],{"class":53},[43,1923,1924,1927],{"class":45,"line":81},[43,1925,1926],{"class":53},"    c.count",[43,1928,138],{"class":49},[43,1930,1931],{"class":45,"line":87},[43,1932,144],{"class":53},[43,1934,1935],{"class":45,"line":94},[43,1936,91],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":90},[43,1938,1939,1941,1944],{"class":45,"line":106},[43,1940,97],{"class":49},[43,1942,1943],{"class":63}," main",[43,1945,103],{"class":53},[43,1947,1948,1951,1953,1956,1958],{"class":45,"line":118},[43,1949,1950],{"class":53},"    c ",[43,1952,407],{"class":49},[43,1954,1955],{"class":49}," &",[43,1957,1843],{"class":63},[43,1959,1960],{"class":53},"{}\n",[43,1962,1963,1965,1967],{"class":45,"line":132},[43,1964,450],{"class":49},[43,1966,100],{"class":63},[43,1968,1969],{"class":53},"(c)\n",[43,1971,1972,1974,1976],{"class":45,"line":141},[43,1973,450],{"class":49},[43,1975,100],{"class":63},[43,1977,1969],{"class":53},[43,1979,1980],{"class":45,"line":147},[43,1981,144],{"class":53},[14,1983,1984,1985,1987],{},"::\nNow both goroutines share the same ",[18,1986,1843],{}," (and the same mutex), and the lock works.",[14,1989,1990,1993,1994,225,1997,225,2000,2003,2004,2006],{},[1117,1991,1992],{},"The lesson",": mutexes (and ",[18,1995,1996],{},"WaitGroup",[18,1998,1999],{},"Once",[18,2001,2002],{},"Cond",") mustn't be copied. Pass structs containing them by pointer, and use pointer receivers for methods that lock. ",[18,2005,1872],{}," catches copy-of-lock bugs.",[23,2008,2009],{"id":1832},"Summary",[14,2011,2012,2013,225,2016,2018,2019,2021,2022,2024,2025,2027,2028,2030,2031,2034,2035,2038],{},"You can now use ",[18,2014,2015],{},"Mutex",[18,2017,360],{}," for mutual exclusion, ",[18,2020,1996],{}," for waiting on goroutines, ",[18,2023,1999],{}," for lazy singletons, ",[18,2026,2002],{}," for condition variables, ",[18,2029,1102],{}," for object reuse, and ",[18,2032,2033],{},"Map"," for concurrent maps — while avoiding the copy-a-mutex and Add-inside-goroutine traps. Next: ",[18,2036,2037],{},"context"," — Go's cancellation and scoping mechanism.",[2040,2041,2042],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .sCrzJ, html code.shiki .sCrzJ{--shiki-default:#E36209;--shiki-github-dark:#FFAB70}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .sMKGj, html code.shiki .sMKGj{--shiki-default:#B31D28;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-github-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-github-dark-font-style:italic}",{"title":39,"searchDepth":57,"depth":57,"links":2044},[2045,2047,2049,2051,2053],{"id":25,"depth":57,"text":2046},"sync.Mutex — Mutual Exclusion",{"id":371,"depth":57,"text":2048},"sync.WaitGroup — Wait for Goroutines",{"id":708,"depth":57,"text":2050},"sync.Cond — Condition Variable",{"id":1123,"depth":57,"text":2052},"sync.Map — Concurrent Map",{"id":1832,"depth":57,"text":2009},"Channels are great for \"communicate by sharing,\" but sometimes you need lower-level primitives: mutexes, wait groups, once. The sync package provides them.","md",{},"\u002Fgo\u002F19-sync-package",{"title":5,"description":2054},"go\u002F19-sync-package","SMY1xb2e6DtCnb3QYYErIaid2bnbiikr1lWKMokn-t8",1786943181886]